  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Chad Protection - NRC Strategic Partnership Agreement</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Flyktninghjelpen/NRC in Chad address immediate needs of most vulnerable refugees in newly established camps and, if conditions allow, in informal sites along border areas. NRC aims at providing access to life-saving assistance and essential services to the most vulnerable displacement-affected populations. A multi-sectoral response, prioritising education, shelter, and ICLA is the core of the program, with livelihood and WASH integrated activities when relevant. Rapid response capacities is also be maintained, in order to deliver emergency assistance (mostly shelters) in case of massive arrivals in the targeted locations. Sectors include Information, counselling and legal assistance (ICLA) and Protection from violence (PfV). The project design is informed by a gender analysis and all indicators are disaggregated by sex.</narrative>
  </description>
